// =====================================================================
// SETTINGS — already implemented in prisma/schema.prisma as a key/value
// store. This file is a REFERENCE ONLY; do not migrate it (it would
// duplicate the existing `model Setting`).
//
// Active model (in schema.prisma):
//
//   model Setting {
//     key       String   @id  // "TAX_RATE", "DELIVERY_BASE_FEE",
//                             // "DELIVERY_FEE_PER_KM", "DELIVERY_FREE_KM"
//     value     String
//     updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt
//   }
//
// Why key/value: new tunables (service charge, min order, etc.) can be
// added without a migration. Defaults live in env (config/env.ts) and are
// seeded via settings.service.seedDefaultSettings(). Reads go through
// settings.service.getSettings(); pricing/checkout call getSetting(key).
//
// Access (settings.routes.ts):
//   GET  /api/settings              Staff+        read all settings
//   PUT  /api/settings/tax          Super Admin   { value: 0.07 }
//   PUT  /api/settings/delivery-fee Super Admin   { baseFee?, feePerKm?, freeKm? }
// =====================================================================
